---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About — Going Native" description="Going Native builds open-source desktop applications with Rust and GPUI." />
		<style>
			main {
				max-width: 720px;
				padding: 3em 1em;
			}
			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 0.25em;
			}
			p {
				max-width: 34em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>

			<p>
				Going Native builds open-source desktop applications with Rust and GPUI.
				The project started from a simple observation: AI coding assistants have
				collapsed the cost of writing native software. Electron was always a
				compromise. It stopped being one worth making.
			</p>

			<p>
				GPUI is a GPU-accelerated UI framework built by the team behind <a href="https://zed.dev/">Zed</a>.
				It's fast, it runs on the metal, and its model will feel familiar to
				anyone who's written React. That's the bet: native desktop apps, built
				with modern tooling, at a fraction of the cost that used to be required.
			</p>

			<p>
				All projects are open-source. Contributions are welcome.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
